---
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
export const prerender = true;

const updated = 'September 28, 2026';
const domain = 'freecrochetbags.com';
---

<TextPage title="Terms of Service" eyebrow="Legal" description={`The terms for using ${SITE.name} and its free crochet patterns.`}>
  <p><em>Last updated: {updated}</em></p>
  <p>
    Welcome to {SITE.name}! These terms apply to your use of <strong>{domain}</strong> (the "site"). By using the site,
    you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Using our patterns</h2>
  <p>All patterns on {SITE.name} are free for personal use. Here's what that means:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>You may</strong> make items from our patterns for yourself, as gifts, or for charity.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>You may</strong> sell finished items you make from our patterns, such as at craft fairs or online shops.
      A credit and link back to the original pattern is always appreciated.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>You may</strong> share a link to a pattern, or one photo with a link back to the pattern page.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>You may not</strong> copy, republish, translate, sell or distribute the written patterns, photos or other
      content, in whole or in part, including as PDFs, on other websites or on social media, without our written
      permission.
    </li>
    <li><strong>You may not</strong> claim our patterns or photos as your own.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Unless stated otherwise, all content on the site, including patterns, text, photos, graphics, the logo and the
    {SITE.name} name, belongs to {SITE.name} and is protected by copyright and other laws. These terms do not give you any
    ownership of our content.
  </p>

  <h2>Newsletter and contact form</h2>
  <p>
    When you subscribe or send us a message, please give accurate information and don't send spam, abusive or illegal
    content. We may ignore or delete messages that break these rules. How we handle your information is explained in our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>When using the site, you agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>break any law or anyone else's rights;</li>
    <li>try to hack, overload, scrape at scale or otherwise disrupt the site;</li>
    <li>use automated tools to copy our content.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Safety</h2>
  <p>
    Crochet involves sharp tools and small parts. Please use common sense. Items made for babies and small children
    should be made with care: secure every part, avoid small pieces that could come loose, and always supervise use. You
    are responsible for choosing suitable materials and for the safety of the items you make.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    We write and test our patterns carefully, but results depend on your yarn, tension and skill, and mistakes can
    happen. The site and all patterns are provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. We don't promise that the
    site will always be available or free of errors. If you find a mistake in a pattern, please
    <a href="/contact">let us know</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent allowed by law, {SITE.name} is not liable for any indirect or incidental loss or damage arising
    from your use of the site or its patterns, including wasted materials or time.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    The site may link to other websites, such as yarn shops. We don't control them and are not responsible for their
    content, products or policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time. When we do, we will change the "Last updated" date above. If you keep
    using the site after a change, you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms? Reach us through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
</TextPage>
